# What this module vendors from yadgarhq/proto (D70). buf closes the import graph
# itself, so listing taskapi also brings yadgar/task/v1 (for Task and TaskStatus,
# which taskapi.proto imports) and yadgar/common/v1.
#
# Unlike task/PROTO_PATHS, yadgar/task/v1 is NOT listed here as a second explicit
# path. task lists it because task is a CLIENT of TaskDbService and needs the
# service definition itself — an import closure brings only the messages a proto
# references, not a service another proto declares. gateway is a client of
# TaskService only, so the closure already brings everything it needs; a second
# explicit path would just re-export what --path yadgar/taskapi/v1 already
# exports.
yadgar/taskapi/v1

# Login (D75), enrolment (D73) and attestation (ADR-0488), listed explicitly for
# the same reason task lists yadgar/task/v1: gateway is a CLIENT of IamService, and
# an import closure brings only the messages a proto references, never a service
# another proto declares. Nothing here reaches yadgar/iamdb/v1 — that is iam's own
# upstream, not this one's.
#
# AT v1.6.0 THIS PATH ALSO BRINGS yadgar/telemetry/v1, and no line was added for
# it. iam.proto began importing telemetry.proto — D74 keys a per-user rate limit on
# D67's Kind, and buf breaking's FILE rule means that enum cannot be lifted into
# common.proto — so the closure vendors it. It is on the include path for protoc
# and is deliberately NOT in build.rs's compile list: the reason is written there,
# and the short form is that this crate already gets its Kind from
# yadgar-telemetry, and a second generated copy would be a second type for one
# concept.
yadgar/iam/v1
